## How Financial Websites Block No-Interaction Exploits
To secure a system completely against autonomous threats, defensive engineers enforce strict architectural controls:

   1. Atomic Database Transactions & Pessimistic Locking: Ensuring that when a balance check occurs, that specific database row is locked completely until the deduction is written, rendering multi-threaded race conditions impossible.
   2. Server-Side Truth: Calculating every single currency calculation, price, and tax constraint strictly on the backend based on read-only databases, treating all incoming user parameters as hostile.
   3. Cryptographic Webhook Verification: Requiring strict hash validation and signature checking for every single piece of data entering the network from an external payment partner.

